				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The `Configuration` element(s) contain the individual receiver configurations (configurations are only about what the partner can receive, not what they can send!).

A configuration is the combination of message type, interface type, message format and version.

For example, the combination `AvailabilityRequest - Synchronous - tXML - 5.0` tells you that the TecCom business partner can receive availability requests sent in the format TXML version 5.0 and is able to give you a synchronous response.</xs:documentation>
